     fhir:div "<div xml:lang=\"en\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\" lang=\"en\"><p class=\"res-header-id\"><b>Generated Narrative: CodeSystem ahip-demo-additional-disability-codes</b></p><a name=\"ahip-demo-additional-disability-codes\"> </a><a name=\"hcahip-demo-additional-disability-codes\"> </a><div style=\"display: inline-block; background-color: #d9e0e7; padding: 6px; margin: 4px; border: 1px solid #8da1b4; border-radius: 5px; line-height: 60%\"><p style=\"margin-bottom: 0px\">Language: en</p></div><p>This case-sensitive code system <code>http://ahip.org/demographics/CodeSystem/ahip-demo-additional-disability-codes</code> defines the following codes:</p><table class=\"codes\"><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\"><b>Code</b></td><td><b>Display</b></td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">HEAR<a name=\"ahip-demo-additional-disability-codes-HEAR\"> </a></td><td>Hearing</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">SEEI<a name=\"ahip-demo-additional-disability-codes-SEEI\"> </a></td><td>Seeing (even when wearing glasses)</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">WALK<a name=\"ahip-demo-additional-disability-codes-WALK\"> </a></td><td>Walking or climbing stairs</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">CONC<a name=\"ahip-demo-additional-disability-codes-CONC\"> </a></td><td>Concentrating, remembering, or making decisions</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">DRES<a name=\"ahip-demo-additional-disability-codes-DRES\"> </a></td><td>Dressing or bathing</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">COOK<a name=\"ahip-demo-additional-disability-codes-COOK\"> </a></td><td>Cooking for oneself</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">FEED<a name=\"ahip-demo-additional-disability-codes-FEED\"> </a></td><td>Feeding oneself</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">TOIL<a name=\"ahip-demo-additional-disability-codes-TOIL\"> </a></td><td>Using the toilet</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">ERRA<a name=\"ahip-demo-additional-disability-codes-ERRA\"> </a></td><td>Doing errands alone, such as shopping or visiting a doctor’s office</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">COMM<a name=\"ahip-demo-additional-disability-codes-COMM\"> </a></td><td>Communicating or being understood using your usual language</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">UNDE<a name=\"ahip-demo-additional-disability-codes-UNDE\"> </a></td><td>Understanding when someone speaks in your usual language</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">NONE<a name=\"ahip-demo-additional-disability-codes-NONE\"> </a></td><td>None</td></tr></table></div>"^^rdf:XMLLiteral
